Hi lavaan users,

Does anyone know the syntax for fixing the residual variance of an item in bifactor CFA model to equal 0? I feel like this should be easy to find, but I'm having trouble finding this info in previous posts/other places.

For example, if I wanted to fix the residual variance of item z2 below to 0--what would the syntax would be?

model <- 'g =~x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + z1 + z2 + z3 + z4 + z5 + z6
f1 =~ z1 + z2 + z3 + z4 + z5 + z6
f2 =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5'

fit <- lavaan::cfa(model, data = item.set2,  ordered =
c("x1", "x2", "x3", "x4", "x5", "z1", "z2", "z3", "z4", "z5", "z6"),
std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE, missing = "pairwise", orthogonal = TRUE)

Thank you!

