Hi Keri,

The issue you're facing is that you're modeling categorical indicators of your latent variables. Under the delta parameterization (the default in lavaan) the residual variances are not estimated as part of the model as they are functions of other parameter, thus you cannot fix them to 0. If you use the theta parameterization the residual variances are estimated paramters (but the scaling parameters are functions of other parameters). You can change the parameterization with the parameterization option in the cfa function (so it would be parameterization = "theta")

Alex

