Dear lavaan team,

In my understanding, cross loadings can only be obtained from Structural Equation modeling (i.e. not from CFA). Am I correct? (I read another answer mentioning that CFA can generate cross loading after certain proceures, but I do not really understand the idea. https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/lavaan/cross$20loading|sort:date/lavaan/X_yaIobn7Xo/s1FTUEfhBwAJ <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/lavaan/cross$20loading%7Csort:date/lavaan/X_yaIobn7Xo/s1FTUEfhBwAJ>)

How should I obtain the cross loadings with lavaan?

Code for reference:
model1 <- 'O  =~ o1 + o2 + o3 + o4 + o5
T  =~  t1 + t2 + t3 + t4
G =~ g1 + g2 + g3
P =~ p1 + p2 + p3
P ~ OC + TC + TGC'

fit1 <- sem(model1, data=data)

Thank you in advance for your help.

