Il giorno lunedì 11 marzo 2019 19:23:00 UTC+1, Terrence Jorgensen ha scritto:
> > I'm trying to do simulate a multilevel dataset
>
> lavaan's simulateData() does not produce multilevel data, nor would it be an easy addition.  Supposing you specify your models at each level with population parameters, which can be transformed into model-implied covariance matrices at each level, you would then need additional arguments to specify how many clusters to generate as well as how many observations within each cluster.  You could do this manually:
> specify your between-level population model, and feed that alone to simulateData() to generate the number of clusters you want
> specify your within-level population model, and loop over the clusters (each row from Step 1) to generate a certain number of level-1 units within each cluster (not necessarily the same cluster sizes, but they can be), again using simulateData().  Cluster-level variables will not be part of the Level-1 model.
> Within each cluster, for each Level-1 variable, add the Level-2 component from Step 1 to each corresponding Level-1 component from Step 2.
> Good luck,
>
> Terrence D. Jorgensen
